{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01CPsXbr6ie4hjzdCYjhoHub","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I can see the issue. The failing test is `hslm autograd training step` in `root.zig:173` which calls `trainStep()` and then checks `ft.metrics.step == 1`. Looking at the `trainStep` method in `trainer.zig:248-252`:\n\n```zig\npub fn trainStep(self: *Self, input: []const u16, target: []const u16) f32 {\n    const loss = self.accumulateGrad(input, target);\n    self.metrics.record(loss);\n    return loss;\n}\n```\n\n`trainStep` calls `accumulateGrad` and `record`, but **never calls `optimizerStep`**. The `step` counter is incremented in `optimizerStep` (line 243), not in `trainStep`. So `ft.metrics.step` stays at 0.\n\nThe test expects `ft.metrics.step == 1` after calling `trainStep`, but `trainStep` was changed to only accumulate gradients without stepping. The test at `trainer.zig:383` (\"full trainer one step\") correctly calls `accumulateGrad` + `optimizerStep` separately.\n\nThe fix: `trainStep` should also call `optimizerStep` for backward compatibility, since it's documented as \"One training step: accumulate one sample and step (for backward compat)\"."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":18052,"cache_read_input_tokens":51942,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":18052,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"44d2ecaa-b17e-43c0-bdaa-9bdb8e6b7a9a","uuid":"505caf9c-c9e6-4444-b6c5-6d2d2621830c"}
